  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Core decisions",
      "level": 2,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "programming / coding",
          "target": "programmazione",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Standard, unambiguous.",
          "anchor": "term-programming-coding"
        },
        {
          "en": "developer",
          "target": "sviluppatore / sviluppatrice",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Agree gender with the referent; use the masculine as the generic/plural default.",
          "anchor": "term-developer"
        },
        {
          "en": "tech / tech industry",
          "target": "settore tech",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Natural in Italian tech media; \"industria tecnologica\" is heavier.",
          "anchor": "term-tech-tech-industry"
        },
        {
          "en": "streak",
          "target": "serie",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "A run of consecutive days, as in the learning-platform sense. Flagged low-confidence: real Italian products (e.g. Duolingo IT) render this inconsistently; confirm on first real use.",
          "anchor": "term-streak"
        },
        {
          "en": "pitfall",
          "target": "insidia",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Ordinary word; stands alone.",
          "anchor": "term-pitfall"
        },
        {
          "en": "foot-gun",
          "target": "trappola involontaria",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Idiomatic English term with no clean one-word Italian equivalent; use a descriptive phrase rather than forcing a fixed term, per `global/terms.md`.",
          "anchor": "term-foot-gun"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Values & data types",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "value",
          "target": "valore",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-value"
        },
        {
          "en": "number",
          "target": "numero",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-number"
        },
        {
          "en": "true / false",
          "target": "vero / falso",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Not capitalised in prose. Literals `true`/`false` stay English in code.",
          "anchor": "term-true-false"
        },
        {
          "en": "character",
          "target": "carattere",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-character"
        },
        {
          "en": "integer",
          "target": "numero intero",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "The type keyword (`int`) stays as-is in code.",
          "anchor": "term-integer"
        },
        {
          "en": "float / decimal",
          "target": "numero in virgola mobile",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "This is the standard Italian idiom for floating-point; use _numero decimale_ only for the plain \"has a decimal point\" sense, not the technical float type.",
          "anchor": "term-float-decimal"
        },
        {
          "en": "array / list",
          "target": "array",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "A bare _array (array)_ gloss is unnecessary; where the source `<define>`s it, gloss with a one-line explanation of the concept instead, since the word itself is already English. Plural is invariant: _gli array_. \"vettore\" is a legitimate but linear-algebra-flavoured alternative; do not mix the two in one document. Never use \"matrice\" (means 2D matrix). Exercise prose sometimes says \"list\" informally for the same concept; render both as _array_.",
          "anchor": "term-array-list"
        },
        {
          "en": "dictionary",
          "target": "dizionario",
          "use": "it",
          "anchor": "term-dictionary"
        },
        {
          "en": "element",
          "target": "elemento",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Array element = _elemento dell'array_.",
          "anchor": "term-element"
        },
        {
          "en": "index",
          "target": "indice",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Ordinary word. Plural: _indici_.",
          "anchor": "term-index"
        },
        {
          "en": "key-value pair",
          "target": "coppia chiave-valore",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "The key itself is _chiave_ (an ordinary word).",
          "anchor": "term-key-value-pair"
        },
        {
          "en": "string",
          "target": "stringa",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Unlike some other languages, \"stringa\" is fully native Italian vocabulary, so it is localized rather than kept English.",
          "anchor": "term-string"
        },
        {
          "en": "Boolean",
          "target": "booleano",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Adjective agrees: _booleano/booleana_. The code type name `Boolean` stays as-is in code.",
          "anchor": "term-boolean"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Functions & control flow",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "if statement",
          "target": "istruzione if",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Keep `if` as the real keyword.",
          "anchor": "term-if-statement"
        },
        {
          "en": "condition",
          "target": "condizione",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Ordinary word; stands alone.",
          "anchor": "term-condition"
        },
        {
          "en": "comparison",
          "target": "confronto",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Ordinary word; stands alone. Avoid \"comparazione\", which is rarer and heavier.",
          "anchor": "term-comparison"
        },
        {
          "en": "expression",
          "target": "espressione",
          "use": "it",
          "anchor": "term-expression"
        },
        {
          "en": "operator",
          "target": "operatore",
          "use": "it",
          "anchor": "term-operator"
        },
        {
          "en": "NOT operator / logical negation",
          "target": "negazione logica",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "The `!` symbol and `NOT` keyword stay as-is in code.",
          "anchor": "term-not-operator-logical-negation"
        },
        {
          "en": "statement (executable)",
          "target": "istruzione",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "The imperative sense: a line of code that does something and gets executed.",
          "anchor": "term-statement"
        },
        {
          "en": "statement (logical claim)",
          "target": "proposizione",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "The proposition sense: a claim that is true or false; also a test assertion. Deliberately distinct from _istruzione_ above; never cross-use.",
          "anchor": "term-statement-2"
        },
        {
          "en": "function",
          "target": "funzione",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "The *keyword* `function` in code stays English; the concept in prose is _funzione_.",
          "anchor": "term-function"
        },
        {
          "en": "to call (a function)",
          "target": "chiamare (una funzione)",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Plainer and more beginner-friendly than the equally-correct \"invocare\"; use _chiamare_ consistently.",
          "anchor": "term-to-call"
        },
        {
          "en": "to define (a function)",
          "target": "definire (una funzione)",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Distinct from _dichiarare_ (declare), which is not used for this concept here.",
          "anchor": "term-to-define"
        },
        {
          "en": "parameter",
          "target": "parametro",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Declaration-site name.",
          "anchor": "term-parameter"
        },
        {
          "en": "argument",
          "target": "argomento",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Call-site value. Deliberately distinct from _parametro_ above.",
          "anchor": "term-argument"
        },
        {
          "en": "input (to a function)",
          "target": "input",
          "use": "en",
          "notes": "Kept English in the software sense; _ingresso_ is reserved for hardware/circuit contexts, not used here.",
          "anchor": "term-input"
        },
        {
          "en": "output",
          "target": "output",
          "use": "en",
          "notes": "As above; _uscita_ not used here.",
          "anchor": "term-output"
        },
        {
          "en": "to return (a value)",
          "target": "restituire",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "\"La funzione restituisce 30.\" Not \"ritornare\", which used transitively is a common but linguistically criticized anglicism (standard Italian \"ritornare\" is intransitive).",
          "anchor": "term-to-return"
        },
        {
          "en": "return value",
          "target": "valore restituito",
          "use": "it",
          "notes": "Noun form; matches the verb _restituire_ above for consistency.",
          "anchor": "term-return-value"
        },
        {
          "en": "pure function",
          "target": "funzione pura",
          "use": "it",
          "anchor": "term-pure-function"
        }
      ]
    },
